    "title": "Woman, 81, found dead in her NYC home, person of interest taken into custody - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Zoe Hussain ,\n3 hours ago\nAn elderly woman was found dead in her Queens home on Thursday — and a suspect 35 years her junior was arrested and charged with manslaughter.\nLillie Hill, 81, was found unconscious by police responding to a 911 call inside her home on 146th Street between Sutter Avenue and Rockaway Boulevard in South Jamaica around 3:30 p.m., according to the NYPD.\nNYPD officers work a scene where 81-year-old Lillie Hill was found unresponsive in Queens, New York, Thursday, Oct. 29, 2026. Kyle Mazza/SOPA Images/Shutterstock\nCops took an unidentified person of interest into custody in connection with the case. Kyle Mazza/SOPA Images/Shutterstock\nHill was rushed to a local hospital, where she was pronounced dead, police said.\nCops then took Patricia Williams, 46, into custody, authorities added.\nWilliams was booked on a manslaughter charge.\nThe circumstances surrounding Hill’s death are not immediately known.\nPhotos captured cops stationed outside her fenced home, just blocks away from John F. Kennedy Airport.\nThe Office of the Chief Medical Examiner will determine Hill’s cause of death, and an investigation remains ongoing.\nFor the latest metro stories, top headlines, breaking news and more, visit nypost.com/metro/\n3",
    "summary": "An elderly woman was found dead in her Queens home on Thursday — and a suspect 35 years her junior was arrested and charged with manslaughter. Lillie Hill, 81, was found unconscious by police responding to a 911 call inside her home on 146th Street between Sutter Avenue and Rockaway Boulevard in South Jamaica around 3:30 p.m., according to the NYPD. NYPD officers work a scene where 81-year-old Lillie Hill was found unresponsive in Queens, New York, Thursday, Oct. 29, 2026. Photos captured cops stationed outside her fenced home, just blocks away from John F. Kennedy Airport.",
